# Telegram Bot Patterns

## Handler Structure

Handlers are structs with injected dependencies:

```go
type ExpenseHandler struct {
    expenseService *service.ExpenseService
    mappingService *service.MappingService
    stateManager   *state.Manager
}

func NewExpenseHandler(
    expenseService *service.ExpenseService,
    mappingService *service.MappingService,
    stateManager *state.Manager,
) *ExpenseHandler {
    return &ExpenseHandler{
        expenseService: expenseService,
        mappingService: mappingService,
        stateManager:   stateManager,
    }
}
```

## Command Handler Pattern

```go
func (h *ExpenseHandler) HandleExpensesCommand(ctx context.Context, msg *tgbotapi.Message) (tgbotapi.MessageConfig, error) {
    logger := log.WithMessage(msg)
    log.WithAction(logger, "expenses").Info("user accessed expenses menu")

    reply := tgbotapi.NewMessage(msg.Chat.ID, "")

    // Check authorization
    mapping, err := h.mappingService.GetByUserID(ctx, types.ID(msg.From.ID))
    if err != nil || mapping == nil {
        return h.getUnauthorizedMsg(reply), nil
    }

    // Build response
    reply.Text = "Manage your expenses:"
    reply.ReplyMarkup = tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardMarkup(...)

    return reply, nil
}
```

## Callback Handler Pattern

```go
func (h *ExpenseHandler) HandleCallback(ctx context.Context, cb *tgbotapi.CallbackQuery, action string, subCommands []string) (tgbotapi.MessageConfig, error) {
    logger := log.WithCallback(cb)
    log.WithAction(logger, "expenses_callback").Info("processing callback")

    switch types.ExpenseAction(action) {
    case types.ExpenseActionAdd:
        return h.HandleExpensesAddCommand(ctx, cb.Message)
    case types.ExpenseActionView:
        h.stateManager.End(cb.Message.Chat.ID)
        return h.HandleExpensesView(ctx, cb.Message)
    default:
        return tgbotapi.NewMessage(cb.Message.Chat.ID, "Not implemented"), nil
    }
}
```

## Conversation State Pattern

```go
// Start conversation
h.stateManager.Start(msg.Chat.ID, state.StateExpensesAdd)

// Check state
currentState := h.stateManager.Get(chatID)

// End conversation
h.stateManager.End(msg.Chat.ID)
```

## Bot Router Pattern

The bot router in `internal/bot/bot.go` handles:

1. Message routing (commands vs conversation input)
2. Callback routing (parse command and action)
3. Response formatting (HTML mode)

```go
func (b *Bot) Handle(ctx context.Context, update tgbotapi.Update) error {
    var msg tgbotapi.MessageConfig

    switch {
    case update.Message != nil:
        msg, _ = b.handleMessage(ctx, update.Message)
    case update.CallbackQuery != nil:
        msg, _ = b.handleCallback(ctx, update.CallbackQuery)
    }

    msg.ParseMode = "HTML"
    b.api.Send(msg)
    return nil
}
```

## Callback Data Format

Pattern: `[command]:[action]:[sub_action]`

```go
// Build
data := types.BuildCallbackData(types.CommandExpenses, "add")
// Result: "expenses:add"

// Parse
command, subCommands := types.ParseCallbackData("expenses:add")
// command = "expenses", subCommands = ["add"]
```

## Inline Keyboard Pattern

```go
reply.ReplyMarkup = tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardMarkup(
    tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardRow(
        tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardButtonData("Add", "expenses:add"),
        tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardButtonData("View", "expenses:view"),
    ),
    tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardRow(
        tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardButtonURL("View Sheets", spreadsheetURL),
    ),
)
```

## Unauthorized Response Pattern

```go
func (h *ExpenseHandler) getUnauthorizedMsg(msg tgbotapi.MessageConfig) tgbotapi.MessageConfig {
    msg.Text = "Please configure Google Sheets first using /gsheets command."
    msg.ReplyMarkup = tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardMarkup(
        tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardRow(
            tgbotapi.NewInlineKeyboardButtonData("Configure", "gsheets:configure"),
        ),
    )
    return msg
}
```

## Adding New Commands

1. Add command constant to `internal/types/command.go`
2. Create handler method in appropriate handler file
3. Register in `internal/bot/bot.go` handleCommand switch
4. If has callbacks, register in handleCallback switch
5. Update `project-context.mdc` Commands Reference table
